{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790963614,"nonce":"sfmrHkUxcCE9z51tIXCuE+qcWmk=","title":"Values in the wrong representation: Int in Float fields, nullary enum identity, getClass, hasField on a class, interface ==, bind time","message":"Triage of 28 uncovered wrong-answer rows that printed a pointer, `\u003cunknown type N\u003e`, a denormal or null (four read-only batches). Fixed in this round:\n\n- An Int initializer of a Float field was stored as Int bits: field initializers did not get the `retype_literal_to` a `var` gets (tast/ast_lowering/decls/fields.rs), and a `@:structInit` literal stored values with no Int-\u003eFloat conversion (ir/mir/expr/literals.rs). MIR scalar replacement hid it while the object stayed local. Issue5432, Issue6822.\n- A parameterless constructor of an enum that also has payload constructors mallocs a fresh tag cell per evaluation, so `None == None` compared two addresses. Now one shared read-only cell per tag (`haxe_enum_nullary_cell`). Issue4287, Issue8187.\n- `Type.getClass` read word 0 of any pointer (an anon handle's Arc pointer) and returned -1 for null. `haxe_type_get_class` returns null unless word 0 is a registered class id. Issue8286.\n- `Reflect.hasField(Cls, name)` dereferenced a class value (a 32-bit id) and crashed; it now answers from the class's static field names. Issue6630 (still reads statics as null, a296dc2).\n- `==` on interface values compared fat-pointer addresses, a fresh one per conversion; it now compares the wrapped object (`haxe_iface_identity`). Issue8528/Issue4363/TestInterface still fail on fat pointers inside erased T (5ac2c89).\n- `.bind` on a `Null\u003cF\u003e` receiver fell through to a by-name call; the receiver and bound arguments were read when the bound function was called, not when bound; `f?.bind()` now yields null when called if `f` was null at bind time. Issue11571.\n\nThe causes not fixed here are filed as fb9da12..9db075a (17 issues) and comments on a957716, a296dc2, 4c1d8fb, e16a823. Issue4526 is a target difference: rayzor gives the static-target answer, the row expects the dynamic-target one.","files":null}]}